# verible-verilog-format flags -- SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH, consumed by BOTH:
#   - ~/dotfiles/utils/fmt.sh                         (CLI batch formatter)
#   - nvim conform.nvim (nvim.easy/.../formatting.lua) (<leader>cf / on-save)
# via  verible-verilog-format --flagfile=<this file>.  Edit HERE only; both
# consumers pick up the change with no further edits.
#
# House style: 3-space indent, aligned port declarations + named-port
# connections, 120-column limit (matches AscentLint LINE_LENGTH=120 so the
# formatter and lint agree on wrapping).
#
# Two things alignment will NOT do, both by design in verible:
#   - a line whose formatted width exceeds --column_limit is emitted
#     byte-for-byte unchanged (--try_wrap_long_lines defaults to false), so a
#     long trailing // comment makes a declaration skip formatting entirely;
#   - an alignment group spans every consecutive declaration (blank lines and
#     comments do NOT split it; only a statement like assign/localparam does),
#     and if aligning the group would push any row past --column_limit the
#     whole group is flush-left instead. One wide package type among plain
#     `logic` declarations therefore unaligns the entire run.
--column_limit=120
--indentation_spaces=3
--port_declarations_indentation=indent
--port_declarations_alignment=align
--named_port_indentation=indent
--named_port_alignment=align
--module_net_variable_alignment=align
